+## Backend CI configuration and evidence boundary
+
+The backend quality checkpoint configures native Ubuntu 24.04 and Windows Server
+2025 root and nested-workspace suites for main/integration pushes, pull requests
+and factory-candidate tags. Existing quality tasks run independently after frozen
+environment synchronization; failed tasks still fail their jobs. Aggregate checks
+require every declared prerequisite to succeed, including after cancellation.
+
+These are configured checks, not a record of successful hosted execution. General
+typing configurations still target Windows; Linux-specific QMN typing is separate.
+Ordinary workflows do not run the complete check-integration/check-release or
+qa-verify task trees. Hosted Windows Server is not native Windows 11 workstation
+release evidence. No branch-protection configuration was inspected or changed.
+
+Mutation jobs remain nightly/default-branch only. Pinned Mutmut 3.3 options and full
+classified results are staged/read explicitly; command errors, incomplete results
+and missing target modules fail. The core 68% threshold and advisory QMN survivor
+policy remain. Current kill rates and full mutation execution are unverified.
+
+Source: .github/workflows/battery.yml, .github/workflows/qmn-ubuntu-24.04.yml,
+.github/workflows/skylos.yml and qa/backend-quality/REPORT.md. Existing verification
+metadata above has not been refreshed by this source-level configuration review.
