+## Quality-pipeline regression evidence
+
+The backend quality lane adds controls for candidate-bound coverage paths,
+incomplete/crashed mutation runs and aggregate CI prerequisites. Coverage must
+resolve to the exact candidate source inventory; unrelated absolute or relative
+checkout paths fail. Existing 80% aggregate/per-package floors and exact/chrono
+100% contract floors remain unchanged.
+
+Workflow tests execute actual nightly shell steps against a controlled CLI with
+the pinned Mutmut option contract, and execute the actual aggregate verdict body.
+They establish local command/validation behavior. They do not establish hosted
+GitHub scheduler cancellation behavior, a completed mutation campaign, live-provider
+correctness or component release acceptance. The nested full suite and clean
+composed-candidate native acceptance remain pending. See qa/backend-quality/REPORT.md
+for provenance limits and inherited red gates; do not equate configured CI with
+complete tier-2/3 or component acceptance.
